    },
    "b-40-dx-quirks-from-the-repo-root-a-te-46": {
      "id": "b-40-dx-quirks-from-the-repo-root-a-te-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "From the repo root, a test selector under "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/<name>/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "scripts/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": ".archon/scripts/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " chooses the working directory. Option values stay unchanged, even\nwhen they look like test paths. Paths naming several packages run one package at a time\nand stop at the first failed package. An argument that names no owner fails instead of\nrunning the suite."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-dx-quirks-within-a-package-substr-47": {
      "id": "b-40-dx-quirks-within-a-package-substr-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Within a package, substring selectors expand to matching files and retain the package's\nisolation groups. Every selected group runs, even after another group fails; the command\nreturns nonzero if any group fails. A full run without arguments still stops admitting\ngroups after a failure. Discovery errors, including selected files outside explicit\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "testGroups",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", stop the request before any group starts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-dx-quirks-test-options-are-forward-48": {
      "id": "b-40-dx-quirks-test-options-are-forward-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Test options are forwarded to each group. Name filters ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "-t",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--test-name-pattern",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ")\nare supported only when the request selects one isolation group, preserving Bun's native\nexit result. Requests selecting multiple groups with a name filter fail before tests load,\nwith a diagnostic naming the groups. Root name-filter requests must also select one\ntest owner; multi-owner requests fail before any tests start and name the owners.\nSharding ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "--shard",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") also requires one isolation group and one root test owner, so Bun\napplies the shard to the complete selected inventory. Select files from one group or\nrun each group separately. Load and hook failures still return nonzero. An explicit\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "--reporter=junit --reporter-outfile <path>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " receives one combined report containing all\nstarted groups and repository-root owners, including their failures and aggregate counts. Each failed child also\ncontributes a process error because Bun can omit load failures from its JUnit output;\nthe child output contains the diagnostics.\nAn unreadable or invalid private report fails its group and contributes a runner error\nwithout preventing later requested groups from running. Bun can omit JUnit output on\nsuccessful zero-file runs. An absent report after exit 0 emits a diagnostic and contributes\nno results, preserving Bun's exit code; absence after a nonzero exit remains a runner error.\nThe wrapper cannot distinguish successful zero-file execution from report loss after exit 0."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
